      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2018 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "An electron-donor-acceptor-acceptor (D-A1 -A2 ) triad has been developed that provides the first proof-of-concept for a photoinitiated molecular circuit. After photoexcitation into an optical charge-transfer transition between D and A1 , subsequent thermal electron-transfer from A1.- to A2 is followed by geometric rearrangement in the D.+ -A1 -A2.- charge-separated state to form an ion-pair contact. This facilitates \"forward\" charge recombination between A2.- and D.+ to complete the molecular circuit with an estimated quantum efficiency of 4\u2009% in toluene at 298\u2005K."
      },
